---
import { SPELLED } from "../config";
import { isCapability, SURFACES, toolCount } from "../data/surfaces";
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
import SurfaceGlyph from "./SurfaceGlyph.astro";

/**
 * Two groups, because the difference is total rather than cosmetic and the page
 * used to flatten it.
 *
 * Eleven cards under one heading said "each surface is its own npm package",
 * which was true of eight of them. `screen`, `sound` and `desktop` broker a
 * framework rather than an app: they ship OFF, they each need their OWN TCC
 * grant, and none of them can be an npm package at all. That last point is the
 * clearest argument on the page for why the app exists rather than only the
 * packages, and while the list was flat it was invisible.
 *
 * The split is read from `KIND`, which is generated from `surfaces.json`, so a
 * card cannot end up under the wrong heading by hand.
 */
const apps = SURFACES.filter((s) => !isCapability(s));
const capabilities = SURFACES.filter(isCapability);

/**
 * Counted from the data. This heading used to hard-code "Four" — and note the
 * capital: `SPELLED` is lower-case because its other callers use it mid-sentence,
 * so a heading has to capitalise it rather than render "five surfaces."
 */
const spelled = SPELLED[apps.length] ?? String(apps.length);
const heading = `${spelled[0]?.toUpperCase()}${spelled.slice(1)} surfaces.<br />One bundle.`;
const capSpelled = SPELLED[capabilities.length] ?? String(capabilities.length);
---

<section id="surfaces" class="wrap scroll-mt-20 py-[96px]">
  <SectionHeader eyebrow="Surfaces" heading={heading}>
    Each of these brokers one Apple app, and each is its own npm package, so a host loads only the
    tools it wants — and write tools against Mail and against Reminders are not the same risk. They
    share one bundle and one grant, which is the whole reason they live together.
  </SectionHeader>

  <div class="reveal grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {
      apps.map((s) => (
        <article class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-[16px] border border-rule bg-bg-2 p-6 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
              {/* Our own glyph, never Apple's icon — see SurfaceGlyph.astro. */}
              <span class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-[9px] border border-rule-2 bg-bg text-accent">
                <SurfaceGlyph id={s.id} />
              </span>
              <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-fg">
                {s.name}
              </h3>
            </div>
            <span class="mono !text-accent">{toolCount(s)} tools</span>
          </div>

          <p class="m-0 text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-pretty text-fg-dim">{s.pitch}</p>

          <div class="mt-auto flex flex-col gap-2.5 pt-2">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[12.5px] text-fg-muted">
              <span class="font-mono text-fg-dim">{s.read.length}</span> always registered
              <span class="text-rule-2">·</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-fg-dim">{s.write.length}</span> write-gated
              {s.gated && s.gated.length > 0 && (
                <Fragment>
                  <span class="text-rule-2">·</span>
                  <span class="font-mono text-fg-dim">{s.gated.length}</span> opt-in
                </Fragment>
              )}
            </div>
            <code class="font-mono text-[11.5px] break-all text-fg-muted">{s.pkg}</code>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="reveal mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {
      apps.map((s) => (
        <p class="m-0 text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-muted">
          <span class="text-fg-dim">{s.name} without the grant — </span>
          {s.withoutGrant}
        </p>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="mt-[96px]">
    <SectionHeader
      eyebrow="Capabilities"
      heading={`${capSpelled[0]?.toUpperCase()}${capSpelled.slice(1)} more,<br />switched off.`}
    >
      These broker the system rather than an app, and the contract is different in every way that
      matters. Each arrives <strong class="font-semibold text-fg-dim">off</strong> until you switch
      it on, each needs its <strong class="font-semibold text-fg-dim">own</strong> permission rather
      than the shared one, and none of them is an npm package — nor could be. The grant lives in the
      app, so a published package would hold nothing.
    </SectionHeader>

    <div class="reveal grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {
        capabilities.map((s) => (
          <article class="flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-[16px] border border-dashed border-rule bg-bg-2 p-6 sm:p-7">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
                <span class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-[9px] border border-rule-2 bg-bg text-fg-dim">
                  <SurfaceGlyph id={s.id} />
                </span>
                <h3 class="m-0 font-display text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-fg">
                  {s.name}
                </h3>
              </div>
              <span class="mono !text-accent">{toolCount(s)} tools</span>
            </div>

            <p class="m-0 text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-pretty text-fg-dim">{s.pitch}</p>

            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-col gap-2.5 pt-2">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[12.5px] text-fg-muted">
                <span class="font-mono text-fg-dim">{s.read.length}</span> always registered
                <span class="text-rule-2">·</span>
                <span class="font-mono text-fg-dim">{s.write.length}</span> write-gated
                {s.gated && s.gated.length > 0 && (
                  <Fragment>
                    <span class="text-rule-2">·</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-fg-dim">{s.gated.length}</span> opt-in
                  </Fragment>
                )}
              </div>
              <p class="m-0 text-[13px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-muted">
                <span class="text-fg-dim">Without the grant — </span>
                {s.withoutGrant}
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
